//  Swamp water wets tilled dirt.
//
//  Vanilla lets water (1) and healing water (6) convert tilleddry and stops
//  there. Swamp water (12) is water with a status effect attached and there is
//  no evident reason it should not farm -- this reads as an oversight rather
//  than a decision.
//
//  NOTHING IN THIS MOD CHANGES BECAUSE OF THIS FILE. The watering system reads
//  liquidInteractions off the matmod at runtime and resolves each liquid to its
//  itemDrop, so a new entry here is picked up with no code aware of it. That
//  was the whole argument for reading the matmod instead of hardcoding
//  tilleddry -> tilled, and this is the first thing to prove it.
//
//  Guarded on the entry NOT already existing, so a future vanilla patch adding
//  swamp water itself makes this a no-op instead of a duplicate.

[
	[
		{ "op" : "test", "path" : "/liquidInteractions" },
		{ "op" : "test", "path" : "/liquidInteractions/2", "inverse" : true },
		{
			"op" : "add",
			"path" : "/liquidInteractions/-",
			"value" : {
				"liquidId" : 12,
				"consumeLiquid" : 0.5,
				"transformModId" : 31,
				"topOnly" : true
			}
		}
	]
]
